<node id="11130141" title="Re^5: How to import &quot;global&quot; variables into sub-scripts from main script?" created="2021-03-22 12:29:18" updated="2021-03-22 12:29:18" _doctext_mode="strict"><type id="11">note</type>
<author id="830549">haukex</author>
<doctext field_name="doctext">&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;i&gt;the global variables are all correctly shared among the files--so why wouldn't strict be shared, too?&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Because [doc://strict], [doc://warnings], and many other pragmas have a &lt;i&gt;lexical&lt;/i&gt; scope. If used at the very top of the file, their scope is limited to that file. [doc://do], [doc://require], and [doc://use] create a new lexical scope for the files they execute. Only [doc://eval]ed code inherits the [doc://strict] and other pragmas from the surrounding lexical scope.&lt;/p&gt;
</doctext>
